OCP sets no `node-ip`. On multi-homed hosts (ssh/local provider, bare metal with VLANs) the node registers with the default route's address instead of the address OCP joined it by.

Live 2026-10-31: `ocp node add synapse --provider ssh-default --host 10.230.30.50` -> InternalIP 192.168.0.165 (eno1, default route), unreachable from the CP otho -> Cilium tunnel broken in one direction, no NFD labels, image pull via the ocp-cache NodePort hangs, yet the node shows "Ready" and OCP reports success. By hand: `node-ip: 10.230.30.50` in /etc/rancher/rke2/config.yaml + restart -> everything fine.

Wanted:
- ssh/local provider: when --host / control_planes.host is an IP literal, it goes in as node_ip. For a hostname: resolve it, or leave it out and log a hint (builder's call, say which in the commit).
- An explicit override per node (OCPNode spec / `ocp node add --node_ip`, ocp.yaml control_planes[].node_ip), because "address OCP reaches the host by" is not always the cluster address (jump host, NAT).
- Hetzner: check whether private networks have the same problem (public eth0 = default route, private network on the 2nd NIC); if so, use the same mechanism.
- Join check: after Ready, compare the InternalIP with the expected address and warn on STDERR if they differ.

Needs rex-rancher (node_ip/node_external_ip in config.yaml). Lanes: provider (address source), state (OCPNode spec/params), infra (Rexfile -> Rex::Rancher), apply (node add option, join warning).

Addendum 2026-10-31: after setting node-ip by hand on a node that was already joined, the Cilium agent pod on that node must also be restarted. Until then CiliumNode keeps the old InternalIP, the tunnel from the CP stays broken, and every pull via the ocp-cache NodePort mirror runs into a 2.5 min timeout (containerd 'trying next host … i/o timeout') before falling back to Docker Hub. So setting node-ip at join is the real fix; repairing it afterwards needs a Cilium restart.

